{"name":"Clove","hex":"#876155","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"clove","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very pungent aromatic spice, the unexpanded flower bud of the clove tree.","A clove tree, of the species Syzygium aromaticum (syn. Caryophyllus aromaticus), native to the Moluccas (Indonesian islands), which produces the spice."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of the small bulbs that make up the large, compound bulb in garlic, shallots, or similar plants.","A segment or natural division of a fruit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clove"}],"entries":[{"title":"Clove","blocks":[{"text":"Cloves are the aromatic flower buds of a tree in the family Myrtaceae, Syzygium aromaticum. They are native to the Maluku Islands, or Moluccas, in Indonesia, and are commonly used as a spice, flavoring, or fragrance in consumer products, such as toothpaste, soaps, or cosmetics. Freshly harvested cloves are available throughout the year owing to different harvest seasons across various countries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Syzygium_aromaticum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-030.jpg/330px-Syzygium_aromaticum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-030.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clove"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/ClovesDried.jpg/500px-ClovesDried.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/ClovesDried.jpg/500px-ClovesDried.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dried cloves","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClovesDried.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/The_flowers_of_clove_tree_in_Pemba_island.JPG/500px-The_flowers_of_clove_tree_in_Pemba_island.JPG